{
  "abstract": "Scaling Transformer depth on ClimbMix-400B under a fixed $1.195\\times 10^{17}$-FLOP budget in the small-batch `NorMuon` regime (`accum=2`) reduces an Iso-FLOPs $12$-layer (`12L`, $71.30\\text{M}$ parameters) model to $1{,}318$ steps versus $1{,}906$ steps for `Static 8L` ($50.33\\text{M}$ parameters), yielding $0.984551 \\pm 0.000730$ versus $0.984930 \\pm 0.000406$ validation bits-per-byte (BPB) across $3$ seeds. We evaluate Complementary Microbatch Braiding (`CLB-12L`), a non-cloning two-stage schedule that initializes all $12$ layers at step $0$ (with zero-initialized residual projections and scalar skips $1.0 h_l + 0.1 x_0$) and partitions the $8$ interior blocks into two $8\\text{L}$ `SSSLSSSL` paths $B_0, B_1$ sharing the stem and readout. For $t < g$, the two microbatches per step alternate deterministically between $B_0$ and $B_1$ at $8\\text{L}$ FLOPs before dense $12\\text{L}$ training. Across $56$ runs ($63$ including references), $3$-seed `CLB-12L` ($g=250$, $1{,}394$ steps, $0.9999\\times$ FLOPs) reaches $0.982042 \\pm 0.001392$ validation BPB ($0.981084 \\pm 0.001381$ holdout BPB), improving on $3/3$ development seeds over `Static 8L` ($-0.002889 \\pm 0.001766$ BPB) and `Static 12L` ($-0.002509 \\pm 0.001568$ BPB), though transition recompilation adds $5.8\\text{ s}$ to total process time. Including a fourth confirmation seed (`seed=314`) and an untouched third validation slice, `CLB-12L` ($0.982259 \\pm 0.001216$) and unconstrained `Early G_stack 8L->12L` ($0.981141 \\pm 0.001642$) beat `Static 8L` ($0.985366 \\pm 0.000933$) on $4/4$ seeds ($p=0.0258$ and $p=0.0016$), split $2\\text{--}2$ against each other ($p=0.384$), and beat `Static 12L` ($0.983927 \\pm 0.001383$) on $3/4$ seeds ($p=0.213$ and $p=0.147$), while modal-coupled `Early HSDM` degrades ($0.987579 \\pm 0.001098$). Leaving $B_1$ frozen in Stage 1 degrades both with homotopy ($0.992455 \\pm 0.000311$) and under direct $\\beta=1$ unbraiding ($0.992649 \\pm 0.000335$, $p=0.0096$). Finally, $3$-seed `CLB-12L` versus i.i.d. two-path sampling is unresolved ($-0.000681 \\pm 0.001800$ BPB), while single-seed controls characterize within/cross-branch unbraiding norms and bundled skipped-update freezing.",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Executed 7 new GPU pretraining runs (Batch P2-9, expanding the study to 56 P2 runs + 7 matched P1 references = 63 runs total) and updated the manuscript, figures, and supplement to resolve all 4 referee points and both minor items: (1) Removed the incorrect general multi-layer pairwise Taylor remainder formula in Section 3.2, added the explicit 3-block linear example E_within(beta) = (1+beta)^3 - 1 - 7*beta = 4*beta*(beta-1) + beta^2*(beta-1) demonstrating first-order intermediate residual propagation, and framed the measured relative norms ||E_within||_2/||Delta_lin||_2 and ||E_cross||_2/||Delta_lin||_2 strictly as descriptive transition diagnostics. (2) Removed unisolated causal claims on per-step branch coverage and momentum decay in Section 1, Section 3.3, Section 5.3, and the Abstract: explicitly stated that the 3-seed CLB-12L vs. iid_branch_12L contrast at g=250 is unresolved (-0.000681 +/- 0.001800 BPB, p=0.580, with iid_branch_12L lower on 2/3 seeds) and that rand_perm_12L (0.981031 BPB), iid_skip_12L (0.986015 at g=250, 0.987456 at g=450), and g=450/850 iid_branch_12L are single-seed (seed=42) observations where iid_skip_12L bundles freezing momentum, second moments, and weight decay. (3) Resolved the staged-unfreezing homotopy confound by running 3-seed direct-unbraiding controls p2_single12_m697_g250_nohom_s{42,137,271} (beta=1.0, H=0), which eliminate the transition loss jump (+0.00037, +0.00035, +0.00044 nats) yet still degrade to 0.992649 +/- 0.000335 val BPB (+0.010573 +/- 0.001806 BPB worse than CLB-12L nohom, p=0.0096); also qualified Early HSDM vs. Early G_stack as a bundled 3-factor contrast. (4) Reconciled Section 3.1 with GPT.init_weights and GPT.forward (s = sqrt(3/d) = 0.07655, resid_lambdas = 1.0, x0_lambdas = 0.1 giving h_{l+1} = 1.0*h_l + 0.1*x_0 for zero-readout layers). (5) Fixed the continuous horizon intercept (1316.872) and added a 4th-seed (seed=314) + untouched 3rd-slice (confirm_bpb, 7,077,888 pure epoch-1 tokens) confirmation in Section 5.4.",
